Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  
`date` : filter rows to the calendar years 2019, 2020, 2021 (e.g., WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)=2021)  
`category_name` : group liquor sales by category and pick the “top‑10” categories in 2021  
`sale_dollars` : numerator to compute a transaction’s retail value  
`volume_sold_liters` : denominator to compute the transaction‑level retail price per liter  
`invoice_and_item_number` : row‑level uniqueness (not used in final aggregations but handy for checks)  

Typical conditions  
• Filter a single year:  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `date`) = 2021  
• Ignore rows whose volume_sold_liters = 0 to avoid division‑by‑zero:  WHERE volume_sold_liters <> 0  

Below are ten progressively more complex exploratory queries (each returns at most 20 rows) ending with the final answer.  
All queries reference the only table allowed:

`bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales`

